cd "/Users/shiriky/bob agent/bob-agent-builder" && gh pr review 18 --request-changes --body "## Code Review — [B2] Define screen — 3-field agent builder form

**Summary:** The Define screen is well-structured and production-ready for a PoC. The \`AgentContext\` design is the right call for sharing state across the three steps, and the form UX is clean. Two issues need fixing before merge — one breaks the NavBar fix that was already merged in B1, and the other is a data-loss risk on page refresh.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Must fix before merge

**\`app/app/components/NavBar.tsx\` — reverts the forward-navigation fix from B1**

This branch was cut before the B1 round-2 fixes were merged. The \`NavBar\` here still renders all three step links as \`<Link>\` regardless of whether the step has been reached, so a user on \`/define\` can jump directly to \`/improve\`. The B1 branch already fixed this (future steps render as \`<span aria-disabled>\`). This PR overwrites that fix.

**Fix:** Rebase onto main (once B1 merges) or cherry-pick the NavBar change from B1. The correct implementation is on \`feature/b1-scaffold-nextjs\` at \`app/app/components/NavBar.tsx\`.

---

**\`app/app/context/AgentContext.tsx\` — state is lost on page refresh**

\`AgentContext\` is pure React in-memory state. If the user fills in the Define form, navigates to \`/test\`, then refreshes — all three fields are reset to empty. For a judge demo this is a real risk: accidental refresh wipes the configured agent.

**Fix (lightweight for PoC):** Persist to \`localStorage\` on every \`setAgentDef\` call and rehydrate on mount:

\`\`\`tsx
const STORAGE_KEY = \"agent-studio:agentDef\";

export function AgentProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  const [agentDef, setAgentDefState] = useState<AgentDef>(() => {
    if (typeof window === \"undefined\") return DEFAULT;
    try {
      const stored = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
      return stored ? (JSON.parse(stored) as AgentDef) : DEFAULT;
    } catch {
      return DEFAULT;
    }
  });

  function setAgentDef(def: AgentDef) {
    setAgentDefState(def);
    localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(def));
  }

  return (
    <AgentContext.Provider value={{ agentDef, setAgentDef }}>
      {children}
    </AgentContext.Provider>
  );
}
\`\`\`

---

### 🟡 Medium

**\`app/app/define/page.tsx\` line 21–28 — \`agentInstructions\` is built in the UI layer**

The instruction string (\"You are a helpful AI assistant. You will receive: …\") is constructed in \`handleSave\` in the page component. This is business logic that leaks into the UI: the backend format, prefix wording, and template are all UI concerns now. When the instruction format changes for B5 wiring, it will be changed here rather than in a shared utility.

**Suggested fix:** Move the instruction builder to \`AgentContext\` (a \`buildInstructions(def)\` helper) or to a separate \`lib/buildInstructions.ts\` so the UI just calls it.

---

**\`app/app/define/page.tsx\` line 29 — \`setAgentDef\` replaces the whole object**

\`setAgentDef\` takes a full \`AgentDef\` and replaces the stored value entirely. If \`AgentContext\` gains additional fields in B3–B5 (e.g. last test result), a call from the Define page will silently wipe those fields. Prefer a partial merge:

\`\`\`ts
// in context:
setAgentDef: (patch: Partial<AgentDef>) => void;
// in provider:
setAgentDefState(prev => ({ ...prev, ...patch }));
\`\`\`

---

### 🟢 Low

- **\`app/app/page.tsx\` line 6** — missing \`dark:text-gray-100\` on the home page \`<h1>\`. This was fixed in B1 round-2 but is missing here because the branch was cut before that commit.

- **\`app/app/define/page.tsx\` lines 92–102** — the \`<select>\` for policy document has no \`\"none\"\` / empty option. If a user hasn't consciously chosen a policy, the first item is silently pre-selected. For a demo this is fine, but a small helper text like \"Defaulting to Service Policy\" next to the label would make the choice visible.

- **\`app/app/context/AgentContext.tsx\` line 41** — the default \`setAgentDef: () => {}\` in \`createContext\` is a silent no-op that would hide bugs if \`useAgent\` is called outside \`AgentProvider\`. Add a dev warning:
\`\`\`ts
setAgentDef: () => { console.warn(\"useAgent called outside AgentProvider\"); },
\`\`\`

---

### ✅ Positive observations

- \`AgentContext\` wrapping \`<AgentProvider>\` in \`layout.tsx\` is the correct placement — state survives route changes without prop drilling.
- The three local \`useState\` fields that sync to context only on Save (not on every keystroke) is good practice — context stays stable until the user explicitly commits.
- \`isValid\` guard disabling the Save button until both text fields are non-empty is the right validation approach for a PoC.
- Placeholder text in the inputs (\`\"e.g. A customer complaint email\"\`) maps directly to the challenge's synthetic data — helpful for judges running the demo.
- \`POLICY_OPTIONS\` constant matches \`challenge/data/policies/\` filenames — clean coupling to the mock store." 2>&1

